[{:db/id "q-161136/selection/93d2d2db4b4c14c745d2c49af6b084f449392515cedb0719ca867fc1dfdff9ee" :answer/id #uuid "ee411a12-7121-5d11-b039-e90d7b982af5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-{u}^{2}-3({u}^{2}+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161136/selection/c07ce431f6bfea220461c50064aac63dd59c929b7b2271d325bf7e07f3215b59" :answer/id #uuid "d5415cce-4362-5a7b-b3d5-120c83f84aee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{2}+3(u+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161136/selection/577d2ad4170de229d8c59c258640b5eb22d7efd96c40d01b4e5b264560c14871" :answer/id #uuid "0f5fde31-969b-5310-9f9a-b667063ec479" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-{u}^{2}+3(u+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161136/selection/9a79e74f441d2d741cca79eb60b953a1df1201e585ecd80811b94df4e9d00ce7" :answer/id #uuid "7dba2d87-1b41-574b-8386-b2322851e3bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{2}-3(u+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161136/selection/c115f1c89919c87fecebd4817e1f8b8c5f7c1bda72b31880e827bcdbf9e65839" :answer/id #uuid "88650080-ff06-5391-bde2-f7231cf18b5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-{u}^{2}-3(u-v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161136/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8748ff34-b50d-5ed5-b0d2-e43db88a9f9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161136/selection/577d2ad4170de229d8c59c258640b5eb22d7efd96c40d01b4e5b264560c14871" :answer-field/choices ["q-161136/selection/93d2d2db4b4c14c745d2c49af6b084f449392515cedb0719ca867fc1dfdff9ee" "q-161136/selection/c07ce431f6bfea220461c50064aac63dd59c929b7b2271d325bf7e07f3215b59" "q-161136/selection/577d2ad4170de229d8c59c258640b5eb22d7efd96c40d01b4e5b264560c14871" "q-161136/selection/9a79e74f441d2d741cca79eb60b953a1df1201e585ecd80811b94df4e9d00ce7" "q-161136/selection/c115f1c89919c87fecebd4817e1f8b8c5f7c1bda72b31880e827bcdbf9e65839"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161136" :question/id #uuid "9941799c-dcc8-54d5-9e86-f358295d68a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161136" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}+3yz$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,u+v,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(-{x}^{2}+3yz)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=u+v\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =-(u\\cdot u)+3\\cdot (u+v)\\cdot ({v}^{2}) \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}+3(u+v){v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(-{u}^{2}+3(u+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161136/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161136"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-160711"] :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=xyz$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 1 & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & v \\\\ 1 & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-v)^{2}+(-u)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(xyz)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=v\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =u\\cdot v\\cdot uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161290/selection/026135bdbfbd5648c858c7562f669c12b3eab92a2dfbcca0a471d7e4821a5f74" :answer/id #uuid "0916d5f8-0fe0-513a-ae34-774abafb0c10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(uv+uv)\\sqrt{2{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}-{u}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161290/selection/c6498124c676289c75b48af355632f99439cc76a3d5617dd1c2f71a9631c4a5f" :answer/id #uuid "383bef0b-fc56-5f04-8f13-cd45b1c71f60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(v-{u}^{2}{v}^{2})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+2{v}^{4}+u}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161290/selection/3815ccd081098438cacf19a6d5971114d3ccba9c26514e2e2d2418eb775d7976" :answer/id #uuid "efe80158-a835-5c3d-a1e4-bfab0b122041" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(u+{u}^{2}{v}^{2})\\sqrt{{v}^{2}-4{v}^{4}-{u}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161290/selection/31ffb714f7aeec0af65375fb0fca76a162ae505580f5c490111629cb3b0ac64c" :answer/id #uuid "e8d2c65c-3804-5909-bd87-dca5f06014fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(uv+u{v}^{2})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}{u}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161290/selection/5ca3a2881c518cd15451450ae6e787bb02647ca4a683d0d5a56c5521c586db11" :answer/id #uuid "c6fd63d1-3d43-538b-9169-80496e70e4c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(uv+{u}^{2}{v}^{2})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+{u}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161290/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c36c6317-cb93-593c-bd50-be329034a767" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161290/selection/5ca3a2881c518cd15451450ae6e787bb02647ca4a683d0d5a56c5521c586db11" :answer-field/choices ["q-161290/selection/026135bdbfbd5648c858c7562f669c12b3eab92a2dfbcca0a471d7e4821a5f74" "q-161290/selection/c6498124c676289c75b48af355632f99439cc76a3d5617dd1c2f71a9631c4a5f" "q-161290/selection/3815ccd081098438cacf19a6d5971114d3ccba9c26514e2e2d2418eb775d7976" "q-161290/selection/31ffb714f7aeec0af65375fb0fca76a162ae505580f5c490111629cb3b0ac64c" "q-161290/selection/5ca3a2881c518cd15451450ae6e787bb02647ca4a683d0d5a56c5521c586db11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161290" :question/id #uuid "d2030333-8a52-5a18-a646-be49d309d8ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-161290" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x-{y}^{2}z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨uv,\\,-u,\\,-{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,0,\\,-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ v & -1 & 0 \\\\ u & 0 & -2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}v & 0 \\\\ u & -2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}v & -1 \\\\ u & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2v,\\,2{v}^{2},\\,u⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨2v,\\,2{v}^{2},\\,u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2v)^{2}+(2{v}^{2})^{2}+(u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+{u}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x-{y}^{2}z)\\,{|}_{x=uv\\,y=-u\\,z=-{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =uv-(-u)^{2}\\cdot -{v}^{2} \\\\  & =uv+{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(uv+{u}^{2}{v}^{2})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+{u}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161290/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161286/selection/91d29e4cc7391bb879d815e8fc61cae82443a7113dff16c76820a79b832314c9" :answer/id #uuid "33a00a0e-ab3b-5331-9800-ea0eae6e2581" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+u)\\sqrt{8v}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161286/selection/d2dcff0638601a66b89b4ca39c214a40219263ed8d5c0ea3ae72dd0bba26d229" :answer/id #uuid "16a98401-3809-5ca7-b405-9897bc9b31cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({v}^{2}-{u}^{2}-2)\\sqrt{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161286/selection/d4c1faeb6da6d4b75bf981fbc4184d92ed73ad3036c08ea6c21316533d82d4f9" :answer/id #uuid "55a55a49-a53d-5f4f-8006-c92711673a33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{2}+2v+2u)\\sqrt{8}v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161286/selection/744e66a1e6b45d2e8ddd52f9bde470f6b98f252ec3c79bedfe010d50b7bd5d93" :answer/id #uuid "e2069f29-4d51-5f60-a9dd-fafb3f575ee1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\sqrt{8}u" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161286/selection/0fd9be0fc4349ea9b2397856387e17320dc771b89bc74ea0430a4d38215dbb8b" :answer/id #uuid "4518e3d7-a24f-5ca6-a02e-940fc55f5343" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u)\\sqrt{8}v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161286/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2809c52-243d-56a4-937d-e75412acf949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161286/selection/0fd9be0fc4349ea9b2397856387e17320dc771b89bc74ea0430a4d38215dbb8b" :answer-field/choices ["q-161286/selection/91d29e4cc7391bb879d815e8fc61cae82443a7113dff16c76820a79b832314c9" "q-161286/selection/d2dcff0638601a66b89b4ca39c214a40219263ed8d5c0ea3ae72dd0bba26d229" "q-161286/selection/d4c1faeb6da6d4b75bf981fbc4184d92ed73ad3036c08ea6c21316533d82d4f9" "q-161286/selection/744e66a1e6b45d2e8ddd52f9bde470f6b98f252ec3c79bedfe010d50b7bd5d93" "q-161286/selection/0fd9be0fc4349ea9b2397856387e17320dc771b89bc74ea0430a4d38215dbb8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161286" :question/id #uuid "60828e8e-d700-5ec8-b0aa-d96b2e205b74" :question/math-academy-id "q-161286" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=-x-y-z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2}-{u}^{2},\\,u⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}-{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2u,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}-{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2u & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-2u & 1 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2u \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,0,\\,2v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-2v,\\,0,\\,2v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2v)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(2v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+4{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(-x-y-z)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y={v}^{2}-{u}^{2}\\,z=u} \\\\  & =-u-({v}^{2}-{u}^{2})-u \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u)\\sqrt{8}v\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161286/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161286"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161134/selection/61c9659087852e7da446498088fb6bfd88a0db5471fa2de42445a8cb114b0cbf" :answer/id #uuid "d28bdea0-7ab5-5903-8698-20f181cb2809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{3}{v}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161134/selection/d39d48ace1e042cad1a4afbcb01a7b5415575dea6dea7b0106f2fc8fd550e605" :answer/id #uuid "9b5a051a-6f4f-589f-b410-0ec4c3589f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{5}{v}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161134/selection/bc75aba647ec943a674227dc9b1777bca1d9dc725e3c440bc673dcfeafa0fd90" :answer/id #uuid "bf9f6a1b-525a-5554-a40b-8b6a28f43944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{4}{v}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161134/selection/38b51fc3fe78116dd49726da4f8154eedda638e3156124f251ee553e7894b51d" :answer/id #uuid "cfd612a0-8d9c-551c-a83d-74c0e3cc77e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{3}{v}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161134/selection/e59c52329ac77d1702c0f7d9b92dfe32d220c540a9607645301a57d04966c562" :answer/id #uuid "4b4154ce-01ce-5b7b-87c6-a5a74439cad6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161134/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50efa88f-c9c6-5856-bb71-fac8d3cbf20b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161134/selection/d39d48ace1e042cad1a4afbcb01a7b5415575dea6dea7b0106f2fc8fd550e605" :answer-field/choices ["q-161134/selection/61c9659087852e7da446498088fb6bfd88a0db5471fa2de42445a8cb114b0cbf" "q-161134/selection/d39d48ace1e042cad1a4afbcb01a7b5415575dea6dea7b0106f2fc8fd550e605" "q-161134/selection/bc75aba647ec943a674227dc9b1777bca1d9dc725e3c440bc673dcfeafa0fd90" "q-161134/selection/38b51fc3fe78116dd49726da4f8154eedda638e3156124f251ee553e7894b51d" "q-161134/selection/e59c52329ac77d1702c0f7d9b92dfe32d220c540a9607645301a57d04966c562"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161134" :question/id #uuid "6c502543-bf1e-5bea-aad2-6cc3e7e40f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-161134" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8}u.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8}u.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =({u}^{2}\\cdot {u}^{2})\\cdot {v}^{2}\\cdot {v}^{2}\\, \\\\  & ={u}^{4}{v}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{5}{v}^{4}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161134/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161134"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161245/selection/631278020d4feb6e6637bbf6f3aedefe7a2af6275b863fcbb6dd29a701c97b2d" :answer/id #uuid "60375e2a-1202-52be-a34b-1f875870ad18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "110" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161245/selection/5aa7d5a70efa831a31e6b82f10565bd69bbaa8c894b8c1ee39d98f5fac58a077" :answer/id #uuid "aa61036c-b349-5eb2-850e-9e34e6c22134" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-108" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161245/selection/d3c0414fe7f80a3ac0f26e96bf9da1a677020b78dc0b44e801a71a00a4ae6178" :answer/id #uuid "2818e865-aacf-520e-b3fb-66ac1395debb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-98" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161245/selection/c3c6c459ed4a41e1787e73fcd54c86c54db8639b1d960afc80ba4dad429691c3" :answer/id #uuid "8e396639-84b5-5d60-93bb-7b95894fe0b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161245/selection/d539ebd65f03b0cbd95834835c34f2d4f29803032810546c02767346e131cb29" :answer/id #uuid "6171a222-43eb-5552-b5bd-28fe4adc14d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "102" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161245/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac6045f-f10d-5c2e-803c-777dc2d85fb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161245/selection/5aa7d5a70efa831a31e6b82f10565bd69bbaa8c894b8c1ee39d98f5fac58a077" :answer-field/choices ["q-161245/selection/631278020d4feb6e6637bbf6f3aedefe7a2af6275b863fcbb6dd29a701c97b2d" "q-161245/selection/5aa7d5a70efa831a31e6b82f10565bd69bbaa8c894b8c1ee39d98f5fac58a077" "q-161245/selection/d3c0414fe7f80a3ac0f26e96bf9da1a677020b78dc0b44e801a71a00a4ae6178" "q-161245/selection/c3c6c459ed4a41e1787e73fcd54c86c54db8639b1d960afc80ba4dad429691c3" "q-161245/selection/d539ebd65f03b0cbd95834835c34f2d4f29803032810546c02767346e131cb29"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161245" :question/id #uuid "6953eabe-51c2-5707-bdc8-81201f86f940" :question/math-academy-id "q-161245" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}({x}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=2u+v,\\,y=2u-2v,\\,z=u+2v\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $1\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u+v,\\,2u-2v,\\,u+2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,-3,\\,-6⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨6,\\,-3,\\,-6⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+9+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & ={x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,{|}_{x=2u+v\\,y=2u-2v\\,z=u+2v} \\\\  & =(2u+v)^{2}-(u+2v)^{2} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}-3{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,1\\le v\\le 2},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(3{u}^{2}-3{v}^{2})\\cdot 9\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9{∬}_{D}\\,(3{u}^{2}-3{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{1}^{2}({\\int }_{-1}^{1}(3{u}^{2}-3{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{1}^{2}{[{u}^{3}-3{v}^{2}u]}_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{1}^{2}(2-6{v}^{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =9\\cdot [2v-2{v}^{3}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =-108.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161245/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161245"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161209/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "5575f5ca-705e-5d1a-9bba-b318f0e8163f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161209/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "25516a84-2883-5d3d-bb94-82f4e4939e6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161209/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "f5dc98d4-30c9-5b9d-af5e-eaca980fd49f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161209/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "f1e366e7-559a-53fb-a62e-303d903b7304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161209/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "4d74a339-f8e0-5e1a-8618-2a25f1c89aa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161209/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "871e6b9c-0b0a-5ef3-b5b1-39eb542d31b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161209/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-161209/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-161209/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" "q-161209/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-161209/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-161209/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161209" :question/id #uuid "1b72ebaf-f39f-5b4b-ba7c-0f67ac67a7e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161209" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}(xy+z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y=u-v,\\,z=0\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,u-v,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,-2⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨0,\\,0,\\,-2⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+0+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =xy+z\\,{|}_{x=u+v\\,y=u-v\\,z=0} \\\\  & =(u+v)(u-v) \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 2},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}(xy+z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{∬}_{D}\\,({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}({\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}-{v}^{2}u]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{3}-{v}^{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{v}{3}-\\frac{{v}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2[\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{8}{3}] \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161209/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161209"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161180/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "a24fcb40-40e0-5739-add2-15c37af16fe3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161180/selection/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" :answer/id #uuid "beda7b0b-cab6-511a-91a8-c154d6e274be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161180/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "528b5f6d-c40b-55d9-9945-e0bf793aec28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161180/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "5483b3f1-6862-542b-8fc9-43bec6188124" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161180/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "d3ad9110-af64-582a-9f78-c40a8f87d2e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161180/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "44144f2f-06dd-56c7-89f4-ea8bb96967fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161180/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer-field/choices ["q-161180/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-161180/selection/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" "q-161180/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-161180/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-161180/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161180" :question/id #uuid "dea7f83f-0cb3-5b15-85a0-823d9bdc61c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161180" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}(x+2y-z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,2u+2v,\\,2v⟩\n$$\n\n \nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 2}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=6.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=6.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x+2y-z)\\,{|}_{x=u-v\\,y=2u+2v\\,z=2v} \\\\  & =(u-v)+2(2u+2v)-(2v) \\\\  & =5u+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(5u+v)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =6{∬}_{D}\\,(5u+v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{2}({\\int }_{0}^{1}(5u+v)\\,\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{5{u}^{2}}{2}+vu]}_{0}^{1}\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{5}{2}+v)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6{[\\frac{5v}{2}+\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =6[5+2] \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161180/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161180"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161212/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "f6cf88b4-e158-5f6f-8b8c-f6422a55dce0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161212/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer/id #uuid "80b72a67-48e2-52d4-ac57-ce058a5bb9b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161212/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "3d48da20-0c19-563a-ba9e-82444fd1476d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161212/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "89dba4e9-a196-5d56-af95-db6365b54304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161212/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" :answer/id #uuid "5c8e4cf0-7b57-54e2-9805-a2a3895a05be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161212/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "569525cd-c138-537d-8b1b-0a928f3f6d1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161212/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer-field/choices ["q-161212/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" "q-161212/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" "q-161212/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-161212/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-161212/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161212" :question/id #uuid "d3a84625-f689-5c14-b34d-31e1adaddccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161212" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}2xz\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=u+v,\\,z=2v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,u+v,\\,2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-2,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨2,\\,-2,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =2xz\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=u+v\\,z=2v} \\\\  & =2u(2v) \\\\  & =4uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}2xz\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4uv\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3{∬}_{D}\\,4uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}2u\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}2v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =3\\cdot [{u}^{2}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161212/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161212"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161182/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "1d483a4c-4818-54f9-8bae-e04b62a6dd84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161182/selection/d79808b1304c1856f3712e6e226ade34c7caf51f0407b91d3e2447e1f8a47743" :answer/id #uuid "93201143-676b-5943-ad34-cae45abd9610" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161182/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "68878cb4-6076-57ac-9b51-3524e631ada4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161182/selection/c8cc0193c097b7d38e4091db7b8ea0b55b90f570b6dfeef91f6d5caca670d84e" :answer/id #uuid "b529a114-2d91-5277-9225-a53f6b5cc111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161182/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer/id #uuid "bf558b20-33e7-5dea-bf4f-b75cde440748" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161182/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e12994d2-5098-5bc3-95a2-c1a9fca7185c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161182/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer-field/choices ["q-161182/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" "q-161182/selection/d79808b1304c1856f3712e6e226ade34c7caf51f0407b91d3e2447e1f8a47743" "q-161182/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-161182/selection/c8cc0193c097b7d38e4091db7b8ea0b55b90f570b6dfeef91f6d5caca670d84e" "q-161182/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161182" :question/id #uuid "cf68f847-61df-5703-8a9b-25a6d5822d24" :question/math-academy-id "q-161182" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}6xyz\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,u+v,\\,v⟩\n$$\n\n \nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{3}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =6xyz\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=u+v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =6(u)(u+v)(v) \\\\  & =6({u}^{2}v+u{v}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,6({u}^{2}v+u{v}^{2})\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\,({u}^{2}v+u{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}v+u{v}^{2})\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{u}^{3}v}{3}+\\frac{{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{v}{3}+\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{v}^{3}}{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}(\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161182/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b529430-3406-506c-b67d-c067dfee44d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161182"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12344"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065891/assets/6ad2702c610c5e7d31d07584c6e605467ff25c8474befd433214451169cc1180.png)\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z) = z-y$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u^2, \\: -v, \\: v \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v) \\in D \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2,$ where $u \\geq 0.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $\\| \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\| = 2\\sqrt{2}u.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\| = 2\\sqrt{2}u.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(z-y)\\,{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=-v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =v-(-v) \\\\  & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4\\sqrt{2}uv\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12346"] :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{S} (x-y)\\: \\textrm{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx = u+v, \\qquad \ny = u-v, \\qquad \nz = v\n$$\n\nfor $0 \\leq u \\leq 3$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u+v, \\: u-v, \\: v\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =x-y\\,{|}_{x=u+v\\,y=u-v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =(u+v)-(u-v) \\\\  & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD = \\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq u \\leq 3, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 3\\},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2v\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{∬}_{D}\\,2v\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2v\\,\\text{d}v\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}1\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{3}\\cdot [u]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 9\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =27\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
